WEBVTT

00:01.650 --> 00:05.018
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:05.105 --> 00:08.424
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.475 --> 00:11.894
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.962 --> 00:14.864
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.932 --> 00:18.467
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:18.518 --> 00:21.654
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.722 --> 00:23.272
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:23.323 --> 00:24.690
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.775 --> 00:28.391
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:36.866 --> 00:39.117
Come on, Stewie. Hurry up.
I want to get good seats.

00:39.201 --> 00:41.936
Ugh, I hate going to hear
authors read from their work.

00:41.987 --> 00:44.072
That Dr. Seuss reading
was dreadful.

00:44.140 --> 00:46.307
And when the drugs
stopped numbing the pain,

00:46.375 --> 00:48.309
the sex became
even more violent.

00:48.377 --> 00:49.477
It doesn't rhyme.

00:49.545 --> 00:51.346
The new stuff
doesn't rhyme!

00:52.548 --> 00:54.282
Hey, there.

00:54.350 --> 00:56.418
You a big fan
of Jonathan Franzen?

00:56.485 --> 00:58.636
Oh, my God,
I worship him.

00:58.704 --> 01:00.271
Yeah, yeah, of all
my writing students,

01:00.339 --> 01:01.806
he's probably
done the best.

01:01.874 --> 01:03.174
I'm sorry,
everybody.

01:03.242 --> 01:05.910
Mr. Franzen has informed us
he's not coming.

01:05.978 --> 01:09.214
Like most real authors, he's
too good for this dumb town.

01:09.281 --> 01:10.315
(all groaning)

01:10.383 --> 01:11.983
MAN:
I hate it here.

01:12.051 --> 01:13.852
Well, this crowd
was promised an author.

01:13.919 --> 01:15.837
No!

01:15.905 --> 01:18.022
Oh, well, you know, I guess
I should be getting back

01:18.107 --> 01:19.157
to my dorm anyway.

01:19.241 --> 01:20.291
I've got a short story due

01:20.358 --> 01:21.942
for my creative writing
class tomorrow.

01:22.010 --> 01:23.544
Oh, creative
writing, huh?

01:23.611 --> 01:25.779
Well, if you'd like me to look
it over before you turn it in,

01:25.847 --> 01:27.331
I'd be happy to.
Really?

01:27.399 --> 01:28.815
(giggles)
That'd be great.

01:28.867 --> 01:30.451
Cool, cool,
I'll follow you in my car.

01:30.518 --> 01:31.485
(whispering):
Come on. We're going.

01:31.553 --> 01:33.087
All right,
hold on.

01:33.154 --> 01:35.322
Is this what your parents are
paying all that tuition for--

01:35.373 --> 01:37.191
so you can
(bleep) dogs?

01:44.682 --> 01:47.284
I'll print up for you
what I have so far.

01:47.352 --> 01:48.519
Okay, I'm gonna go
in there with her.

01:48.586 --> 01:50.170
You just sit out here
and be quiet.

01:50.221 --> 01:51.972
Here, watch one of her
movies or something.

01:53.141 --> 01:55.959
<i>Ugh, Charlie St. Cloud?</i>

01:56.027 --> 01:57.895
A-And why are there
so many fingerprints on this?

01:57.962 --> 02:02.032
<i>Who's handling their Charlie
St. Cloud DVD all the time?</i>

02:10.592 --> 02:14.762
Lois, can I have
a Pop-Tart in bed, please?

02:14.829 --> 02:16.497
Lois?

02:16.564 --> 02:17.531
Hey, Chris?

02:17.599 --> 02:19.066
CHRIS:
Yeah?

02:19.134 --> 02:21.752
Do you think Lois would be okay
if I ate a Pop-Tart in bed?

02:21.820 --> 02:22.786
Probably.

02:22.854 --> 02:23.954
Probably, right?

02:24.022 --> 02:26.140
Lois, you in the bathroom?

02:26.207 --> 02:28.292
(gasping)

02:32.630 --> 02:34.865
Well, Mrs. Griffin,
you have three crushed ribs,

02:34.933 --> 02:36.784
but I was able to stop
the internal bleeding.

02:36.851 --> 02:39.620
Doctor, this has happened
seven times in the last month.

02:39.687 --> 02:42.389
Peter rolls over in his sleep
and almost kills me.

02:42.457 --> 02:43.657
I see.

02:43.725 --> 02:44.691
Well, that sucks.

02:44.759 --> 02:46.193
Look, I don't do it
on purpose.

02:46.261 --> 02:48.061
Well, it looks like you got
a handle on it then.

02:48.129 --> 02:49.279
No, we don't.

02:49.347 --> 02:51.148
He practically
smothers me every night.

02:51.216 --> 02:52.549
Well, are you hogging
the blankets?

02:52.617 --> 02:53.750
No.

02:53.818 --> 02:55.502
"Probably hogging
blankets."

02:55.570 --> 02:57.955
And if he's not smothering me,
he's keeping me up all night

02:58.022 --> 03:00.691
writing with that
giant plume of his.

03:00.758 --> 03:04.411
"Dearest Augustine,
I do hope this latest damp

03:04.462 --> 03:05.929
has not aggravated
your gray lung."

03:05.997 --> 03:07.564
Dip, dip, dip, dip, dip.

03:07.632 --> 03:09.883
"Matters stateside
have taken a tragic turn

03:09.934 --> 03:11.935
"as this year's gourd crop
has fallen prey

03:12.020 --> 03:13.854
"to a rather
unexpected infestation

03:13.921 --> 03:15.222
of saltmarsh cutworms."

03:15.290 --> 03:16.406
Dip, dip, dip, dip, dip.

03:16.474 --> 03:18.025
Peter, it's 4:00
in the morning.

03:18.092 --> 03:19.526
Come to bed!

03:19.594 --> 03:22.296
"Marital concerns continue
to bedevil me."

03:25.216 --> 03:27.251
Look, I'm sorry.

03:27.318 --> 03:29.853
I wasn't planning on
spending all night there.

03:29.921 --> 03:32.456
Look, how about if I take
you to the park, huh?

03:32.524 --> 03:35.292
Come on. You like
the park, right?

03:35.360 --> 03:37.611
We're about to
pass the turnoff.

03:37.679 --> 03:40.547
Here it comes.

03:40.615 --> 03:42.533
You may take me
to the park.

03:47.589 --> 03:49.740
Um, excuse me. I didn't
bring any of my toys.

03:49.807 --> 03:51.108
Can I play with
some of yours?

03:51.175 --> 03:53.026
No! Mine!

03:54.546 --> 03:56.914
Are you all right?

03:56.981 --> 03:58.214
I'm fine.

03:58.282 --> 04:00.633
I-I didn't push him back
because he has leukemia.

04:00.701 --> 04:01.701
My name's Penelope.

04:01.768 --> 04:02.668
What's yours?

04:02.736 --> 04:03.803
Stewie.

04:03.871 --> 04:05.571
I've never seen you
around here before.

04:05.639 --> 04:07.907
I'm new to town and I
don't have many friends.

04:07.975 --> 04:09.308
(chuckling):
All right.

04:09.376 --> 04:11.944
A lot of pressure on me
instantly, but okay.

04:11.995 --> 04:14.180
Would you like to play with
some of my toys, Stewie?

04:14.248 --> 04:15.364
Well, what have you got?

04:15.449 --> 04:17.166
I have a set of jacks,
a paddleball,

04:17.234 --> 04:19.035
and this taffy
with superglue.

04:19.102 --> 04:21.170
Isn't that the little
boy who pushed you?

04:21.238 --> 04:22.688
Hmm, yes.

04:22.756 --> 04:26.425
You there, would you like
a piece of candy?

04:30.130 --> 04:31.948
(choking)

04:37.688 --> 04:39.555
Don't push.

04:44.077 --> 04:46.812
Uh, Lois, why do we have
Lucy and Ricky beds?

04:46.863 --> 04:49.715
Because I'm sick of you crushing
me in the middle of the night.

04:49.783 --> 04:51.417
Dr. Hartman called
about my X rays.

04:51.485 --> 04:53.786
He said my spine
is now disfigured.

04:53.854 --> 04:56.188
Lois, if God wanted me
to not sleep with my wife,

04:56.256 --> 04:57.790
he would have made me
John Travolta.

04:57.858 --> 04:59.191
Peter, I'm really
tired, okay?

04:59.259 --> 05:01.093
Just give the bed a try.

05:05.966 --> 05:07.683
There you go.

05:07.751 --> 05:09.268
Good night, Peter.

05:09.336 --> 05:11.404
I can't sleep like this, Lois.

05:11.471 --> 05:13.139
I need someone to cuddle with.

05:13.206 --> 05:15.041
Believe it or not,
men like to cuddle,

05:15.108 --> 05:17.910
even cold, unfeeling men
like Charles Bronson.

05:17.978 --> 05:20.379
Hey, Charles Bronson's wife.

05:20.447 --> 05:23.316
Scooch over.
I want to cuddle.

05:23.383 --> 05:25.484
Mmm, that's nice.

05:30.757 --> 05:31.924
I don't know
what the big deal is.

05:31.992 --> 05:34.393
I stopped for one drink
after work.

05:34.461 --> 05:36.195
Yes, but it's
every night.

05:36.263 --> 05:39.281
There, now you can be
upset about that.

05:39.349 --> 05:40.349
This is fun.

05:40.417 --> 05:41.984
I like playing
with you, Penelope.

05:42.052 --> 05:43.185
What shall
we play next?

05:43.253 --> 05:44.904
Well, let's see
what you have.

05:44.972 --> 05:47.890
<i>You have a pop-up version
of the Unabomber's Manifesto?</i>

05:47.958 --> 05:51.210
Yes, at the end the brother
pops up and turns you in.

05:55.949 --> 05:57.583
What's this
on your Etch A Sketch?

05:57.651 --> 05:59.352
Oh, those are some advanced
mathematical formulas

05:59.419 --> 06:01.020
I've just been
tinkering with.

06:01.088 --> 06:02.421
You're kidding?
I do that, too.

06:02.489 --> 06:04.690
But what are
these formulas for?

06:04.758 --> 06:06.759
For these.

06:14.735 --> 06:15.735
(gasps)
Oh, my God,

06:15.802 --> 06:16.969
you've got a weapons room, too?

06:17.037 --> 06:18.170
And look at the size of it.

06:18.238 --> 06:19.538
It's amazing.

06:19.606 --> 06:21.774
Yes, although sometimes
I think it's too big.

06:21.842 --> 06:24.276
It takes the cleaning woman
forever to clean it.

06:27.948 --> 06:30.249
Was already broken.

06:37.556 --> 06:39.056
My word, Penelope,

06:39.124 --> 06:41.258
you and I seem to have
quite a lot in common.

06:41.326 --> 06:42.660
Do you actually
use these?

06:42.728 --> 06:45.229
Only when fear, spite, jealousy,
and revenge demand.

06:45.297 --> 06:47.665
<i>I bought that to kill the women
from Sex and the City,</i>

06:47.733 --> 06:50.267
but time seems
to be doing it for me.

06:50.335 --> 06:52.103
(gasps)
You're wicked.

06:52.170 --> 06:53.704
Do your parents
have any idea?

06:53.772 --> 06:54.839
My mother's
not a concern.

06:54.906 --> 06:56.023
I don't really have
to worry

06:56.091 --> 06:57.375
about her anymore.

06:57.442 --> 07:00.244
Oh, do you have one of those
white wine zombie moms?

07:00.312 --> 07:01.479
No, she died.

07:01.546 --> 07:02.763
She was taking a tub

07:02.831 --> 07:05.132
and somebody came in
and cut her head off.

07:05.200 --> 07:06.567
Wait a moment.

07:06.635 --> 07:09.437
Did... did you kill her?

07:09.504 --> 07:13.374
Well, I held the knife...
and her hair.

07:13.442 --> 07:16.777
Oh, my God, I've been dreaming
about doing that for years,

07:16.845 --> 07:18.813
and you've actually gone ahead
and done it.

07:18.880 --> 07:20.531
Penelope...

07:20.599 --> 07:22.299
I've never said this
to anyone before,

07:22.367 --> 07:25.803
but I feel like I may have
finally found, in you,

07:25.871 --> 07:28.139
my one true soul mate.

07:28.206 --> 07:29.507
Do you feel this way, too?

07:29.574 --> 07:31.075
I do, Stewart.

07:31.143 --> 07:33.544
It's as if our meeting were
more than a mere coincidence.

07:33.612 --> 07:36.013
It's as if we were
meant to be together.

07:36.081 --> 07:37.281
Indeed.

07:37.349 --> 07:39.850
This must be how Maverick felt
when he met Goose.

07:39.918 --> 07:41.418
I feel the need.

07:41.470 --> 07:43.604
The need for speed.
The need for speed.

07:43.688 --> 07:45.489
And Scientology.
No, just speed.

07:49.060 --> 07:51.112
So, listen, Quagmire,
there's something

07:51.196 --> 07:52.997
I kind of wanted
to talk to you about.

07:53.064 --> 07:56.133
E-Ever since Lois got us
twin beds, I can't fall asleep.

07:56.201 --> 07:58.035
I'm used to having
another person there.

07:58.103 --> 08:00.221
I know. I always sleep better
when I'm next to someone.

08:00.288 --> 08:01.222
Yeah, it's only
natural, right?

08:01.289 --> 08:02.590
I'm glad to hear
you say that

08:02.657 --> 08:05.276
'cause, you know, I guess
what I'm trying to say is,

08:05.343 --> 08:08.245
I... want to propose
an arrangement

08:08.313 --> 08:10.297
that could benefit
the both of us.

08:10.365 --> 08:11.599
Okay.

08:11.666 --> 08:13.868
Men need someone to spoon with
and snuggle with

08:13.935 --> 08:18.606
just the same as women, and when
you don't have that, it-it's...

08:18.673 --> 08:20.591
I... well,
what I'm getting at is...

08:21.927 --> 08:25.896
I would like for you
to sleep with me in my bed,

08:25.964 --> 08:28.299
and this, this is not about sex;
it's about sleep.

08:28.366 --> 08:29.583
No, no, I totally
get it, Peter.

08:29.651 --> 08:30.918
Snuggling is a
basic human need.

08:30.986 --> 08:33.187
Right, I mean, who says
that the body next to you

08:33.255 --> 08:34.855
has to be male or female
or... whatever?

08:34.923 --> 08:35.890
Or alive.

08:35.957 --> 08:37.958
Yeah... well, no,
but, yeah.

08:38.026 --> 08:39.426
Look, I, I think
it's a great idea

08:39.494 --> 08:40.694
and I, I'm completely with you.

08:40.762 --> 08:42.029
I'm in. Let's try it.

08:42.097 --> 08:44.498
Yay, that is
such good news.

08:44.566 --> 08:46.450
And I'm so happy
they gave us a booth.

08:46.518 --> 08:47.818
I know, 'cause they're
supposed to be reserved

08:47.886 --> 08:48.853
for parties of
three or more.

08:48.920 --> 08:50.054
I know!

08:53.208 --> 08:55.960
Oh, Stewie, it's so nice
to finally have someone

08:56.027 --> 08:57.361
to do naughty
things with.

08:57.429 --> 08:58.462
Definitely.

08:58.530 --> 08:59.897
All right, I made
a wallet bomb

08:59.965 --> 09:01.298
and I planted it
on Mort.

09:01.349 --> 09:03.734
As soon
as he opens it-- boom.

09:06.104 --> 09:09.273
(both giggling)

09:13.677 --> 09:15.011
Oh, bloody hell.

09:15.062 --> 09:17.530
How do you go two weeks
without opening your wallet?

09:17.615 --> 09:19.566
Yeah, he's been out
to dinner, like, four times.

09:19.650 --> 09:21.818
We're clearly not going
to get him this way.

09:21.869 --> 09:24.537
I know, which is why
I just planted another bomb

09:24.622 --> 09:27.540
that's set to go off every time
he burps into his hand.

09:27.625 --> 09:29.742
(stifled burp)

09:32.746 --> 09:36.299
Ohh, I'd better make sure
my wallet's okay.

09:41.689 --> 09:43.790
I say, we're
on quite a run.

09:43.857 --> 09:45.358
We blew up the
Great Wall of China,

09:45.426 --> 09:47.594
bombed the Eiffel Tower, a
look at this note I sent off.

09:47.661 --> 09:49.762
"Dear Pakistan,
Up yours.

09:49.830 --> 09:51.231
Love, India."

09:51.298 --> 09:52.632
Let's see
what happens.

09:58.138 --> 09:59.973
They did not need much.

10:00.040 --> 10:02.275
All right,
Stewie, your turn.

10:02.343 --> 10:05.461
Okay, I have to destroy
Copenhagen with a...

10:05.529 --> 10:08.164
tidal wave,
and the theme is...

10:08.231 --> 10:09.649
the Roaring Twenties.

10:09.717 --> 10:12.285
Tha-That's, that's,
that's a challenge.

10:16.457 --> 10:20.176
("Charleston" playing)

10:20.243 --> 10:23.162
Roarin' twenten tidal waven!

10:31.822 --> 10:33.056
Peter, what's
going on?

10:33.123 --> 10:34.891
Quagmire's having
a sleepover with me.

10:34.942 --> 10:36.309
You can't
be serious.

10:36.377 --> 10:38.011
Look, Lois, I told you
that I need

10:38.078 --> 10:40.046
to have somebody
sleeping next to me.

10:40.114 --> 10:41.481
All right, now if that's
not going to be you...

10:41.548 --> 10:43.016
Fine. Do what you want.

10:43.083 --> 10:45.234
I don't care,
but I think it's very strange.

10:45.286 --> 10:46.569
Okay, that's the
one thing it's not.

10:46.637 --> 10:47.937
Yeah, it's not strange.

10:48.005 --> 10:50.823
I already told you:
I don't care.

10:50.891 --> 10:52.158
It's not strange.

10:52.226 --> 10:53.359
I know.

10:53.427 --> 10:54.494
All right,
let's see here.

10:54.561 --> 10:57.163
Now just, uh, wrap
yourself around me.

10:57.231 --> 10:58.398
Is that okay?

10:58.465 --> 11:00.266
Yeah, actually, you can
hold me even tighter.

11:00.334 --> 11:03.670
Okay, I just need to put
this arm right around here.

11:03.737 --> 11:05.321
Yeah, there we go.

11:05.389 --> 11:08.324
Good, now let's just
fall asleep like this.

11:09.693 --> 11:11.661
Your boxers are
a little starchy.

11:11.729 --> 11:13.196
Can I take 'em off
with my foot?

11:13.263 --> 11:15.098
Sure.

11:19.586 --> 11:22.221
Come on, you.

11:28.812 --> 11:30.213
Good evening.
I'm Tom Tucker.

11:30.280 --> 11:32.281
Our top story:
Authorities are still searching

11:32.349 --> 11:35.151
for the culprits in a series
of horrific acts of destruction

11:35.219 --> 11:37.387
all across-- scroll down, guys--

11:37.454 --> 11:38.855
the globe.

11:38.922 --> 11:40.156
That could've fit on there.

11:40.224 --> 11:41.958
There was a long space
at the end of that line.

11:42.026 --> 11:44.010
My God, it's you,
isn't it?

11:44.094 --> 11:45.294
It's you and Penelope

11:45.346 --> 11:46.963
who've been doing
all of these horrible things.

11:47.031 --> 11:48.481
So? I've always been
about world domination.

11:48.549 --> 11:50.816
What the hell did you think
I was talking about when I said,

11:50.883 --> 11:52.250
"Victory shall be mine"?

11:52.318 --> 11:54.286
You have not said that
in a very long time.

11:54.354 --> 11:55.554
Well, I'm back on it.

11:55.621 --> 11:58.223
Stewie, Penelope is taking you
down a dark path.

11:58.291 --> 12:00.142
Look, in the past
you've done terrible things,

12:00.193 --> 12:01.610
but it's always been
about the pursuit

12:01.678 --> 12:03.578
of your greater goal
of world domination.

12:03.646 --> 12:07.215
But this girl-- she just creates
chaos for the sake of chaos.

12:07.283 --> 12:08.350
So, what are you saying?

12:08.418 --> 12:09.985
I'm saying she's
a bad influence on you,

12:10.053 --> 12:11.620
and you should stop spending
time with her.

12:11.688 --> 12:12.888
I shall do no such thing.

12:12.955 --> 12:14.456
Penelope is wonderful.

12:14.524 --> 12:15.924
We're going to be
together forever.

12:17.960 --> 12:20.212
Well, Rupert,
this is a big mess.

12:20.296 --> 12:22.264
What the hell were you
doing talking to him?

12:28.071 --> 12:29.938
You know who I think
is an ugly slut?

12:30.006 --> 12:31.039
Miss Sharon.

12:31.107 --> 12:32.541
Miss Sharon
from your day care?

12:32.608 --> 12:33.608
Yes.

12:33.676 --> 12:35.377
This is a map of her house.

12:35.445 --> 12:36.745
I thought we could
burn her in her bed

12:36.813 --> 12:37.879
while her children watch.

12:37.947 --> 12:39.314
You know, Penelope,

12:39.382 --> 12:42.117
maybe we don't have
to kill someone every day.

12:42.185 --> 12:44.302
There are other things to do.

12:44.370 --> 12:45.220
Like what?

12:45.288 --> 12:46.354
I-I don't know.

12:46.422 --> 12:47.989
You know what? Forget it.

12:48.057 --> 12:50.442
I-I think Brian just got
in my head a bit. That's all.

12:50.510 --> 12:51.610
Brian?

12:51.677 --> 12:53.378
Why? What did Brian say?

12:53.446 --> 12:54.646
Oh, nothing.

12:54.714 --> 12:57.015
He just thinks that you're
a bad influence on me.

12:57.083 --> 12:59.017
(chuckles) T-Thinks I should stop
seeing you.

12:59.085 --> 13:00.318
He does?

13:00.386 --> 13:02.237
How dare he!

13:02.305 --> 13:03.472
Babe? Babe?

13:03.539 --> 13:04.739
Don't worry about it,
all right?

13:04.791 --> 13:07.092
Stewart, do you love me?

13:07.160 --> 13:08.627
More than anything.

13:08.694 --> 13:10.962
Then swear on that love
that you'll do what I ask.

13:11.030 --> 13:12.164
Just name it.

13:12.231 --> 13:13.832
Kill him.

13:13.900 --> 13:15.534
Kill Brian for me.

13:15.601 --> 13:17.919
(soap opera-like musical sting)

13:17.970 --> 13:19.141
<i>SOAP OPERA ANNOUNCER:
Family Guy is brought to you</i>

13:19.166 --> 13:21.166
<i>by AXE Body Spray.</i>

13:21.390 --> 13:23.892
<i>AXE Body Spray:
Spray it on after gym class</i>

13:23.960 --> 13:25.977
<i>instead of getting beat up
in the shower.</i>

13:26.045 --> 13:28.330
<i>Kind of weird those guys
want to fight you naked, huh?</i>

13:28.397 --> 13:29.498
<i>AXE Body Spray.</i>

13:37.420 --> 13:39.755
Oh, God, I can't kill Brian.

13:39.823 --> 13:41.123
Even for Penelope.

13:41.190 --> 13:43.242
He's my dog, my friend.

13:43.309 --> 13:44.743
Well, I wonder what words

13:44.811 --> 13:46.962
are gonna come
out of this pen today.

13:47.030 --> 13:48.397
All right, I can do this.

14:01.811 --> 14:03.212
(grunts)

14:08.251 --> 14:10.018
Oh, who am I kidding?

14:10.086 --> 14:11.637
I can't do this.

14:11.704 --> 14:13.205
(sneezes)

14:22.332 --> 14:26.085
♪ You're lookin'
kind of lonely, girl ♪

14:26.169 --> 14:30.671
♪ Would you like someone new
to talk to? ♪

14:30.739 --> 14:33.674
♪ Oh, yeah, all right ♪

14:33.742 --> 14:37.178
♪ I'm feelin'
kind of lonely, too ♪

14:37.246 --> 14:38.963
♪ If you don't mind ♪

14:39.047 --> 14:43.167
♪ Can I sit down here
beside you? ♪

14:43.235 --> 14:46.404
♪ Oh, yeah, all right ♪

14:46.472 --> 14:50.425
♪ If I seem
to come on too strong ♪

14:50.492 --> 14:53.227
♪ I hope that
you will understand ♪

14:53.278 --> 14:55.730
♪ I say these things
'cause I'd like to know ♪

14:55.781 --> 14:58.950
♪ If you're as lonely as I am ♪

14:59.017 --> 15:03.621
♪ And if you'd mind sharing
the night together ♪

15:03.689 --> 15:06.507
♪ Oh, yeah ♪

15:06.575 --> 15:09.727
♪ Sharing the night together ♪

15:09.795 --> 15:12.964
♪ Whoa-oh, yeah... ♪

15:15.434 --> 15:18.069
I don't care how many children
you've lost in childbirth.

15:18.137 --> 15:19.670
You're fired.

15:19.738 --> 15:21.272
(Cockney accent):
But I was only having a child

15:21.340 --> 15:22.707
because you
and the mister...

15:22.774 --> 15:26.844
You don't get to speak
of me and the mister!

15:26.912 --> 15:29.096
Ah, Stewie.
So did you do it?

15:29.164 --> 15:31.966
Have you removed that wretched
cur from our existence?

15:32.034 --> 15:34.569
I just couldn't bring myself
to kill him, Penelope.

15:34.636 --> 15:36.871
Brian is my best friend.

15:36.939 --> 15:38.439
Perhaps you're right.

15:38.507 --> 15:40.641
Perhaps it was wrong of me
to ask you to do such a thing.

15:40.709 --> 15:42.210
Oh, thank you.

15:42.277 --> 15:44.545
I'm so glad you're being
so understanding about this.

15:44.613 --> 15:47.114
I was actually dreading
having to tell you about this.

15:47.182 --> 15:48.716
Bleah.

15:48.784 --> 15:51.152
It appears I'll have
to kill him myself.

15:51.220 --> 15:52.286
What?!

15:52.354 --> 15:54.288
I knew you were too weak
to do this.

15:54.389 --> 15:55.756
You're nothing but a coward.

15:55.824 --> 15:57.608
No, Penelope, wait!

15:57.676 --> 16:00.061
(groans) Strong women always
turn out to be nightmares.

16:00.128 --> 16:01.762
Like Joan of Arc.

16:01.830 --> 16:04.332
Hey, guys,
I'm not like other girls.

16:04.399 --> 16:06.934
I kill people and burp
and watch so much porn.

16:07.002 --> 16:08.836
Isn't that cool?
No.

16:08.904 --> 16:10.538
I like a lot
of goofball comedies

16:10.606 --> 16:12.273
that other chicks don't like.

16:12.341 --> 16:14.809
<i>My favorite thing to play
is Call of Duty.</i>

16:14.877 --> 16:17.945
Look me up.
I'm GuitarGurrrl76.

16:18.013 --> 16:19.513
Let's burn this chick
at the stake.

16:19.565 --> 16:20.781
I love steak!

16:20.849 --> 16:21.949
Other girls don't.

16:22.017 --> 16:23.618
I'm actually more like a dude.

16:23.685 --> 16:25.203
Hey, guys,
don't come in my room.

16:25.287 --> 16:27.638
I might be rubbin' one in.

16:30.826 --> 16:33.027
Peter, this is ridiculous.

16:33.095 --> 16:34.795
It's time for you
to come home.

16:34.863 --> 16:36.297
I live here now, Lois.

16:36.365 --> 16:38.866
Look, I'm sorry
that I ever got us separate...

16:38.934 --> 16:40.301
Is that a bracelet
you're wearing?

16:40.368 --> 16:41.752
It's a giggity band, Lois.

16:41.820 --> 16:43.221
You wouldn't understand.

16:43.288 --> 16:44.822
Look, Peter,
if you come home now,

16:44.890 --> 16:46.324
we can get our old bed back,

16:46.391 --> 16:48.292
and you can snuge with me
as much as you want.

16:48.360 --> 16:49.727
Well...

16:49.795 --> 16:51.529
You promise?

16:51.597 --> 16:52.997
I promise.

16:53.065 --> 16:56.367
'Cause, you know,
I missed cuddling with you, too.

16:56.435 --> 16:57.368
You did?

16:57.436 --> 16:59.270
I sure did.

16:59.338 --> 17:01.522
Well, then, hey...

17:01.590 --> 17:03.941
what do you say we go home, huh?

17:04.009 --> 17:06.109
Sounds good to me.

17:06.177 --> 17:10.030
(gasping)

17:13.701 --> 17:15.802
Oh, Brian, there you are!

17:15.870 --> 17:17.037
Thank God.
Oh, hey, Stewie.

17:17.088 --> 17:18.371
Did you make that coffee?

17:18.439 --> 17:20.040
Um, no, it was here
when I came in.

17:20.107 --> 17:22.175
I assume Lois made it.
Don't drink that!

17:22.243 --> 17:24.444
Hey, that mug was my crew
gift from "Class Holes."

17:24.512 --> 17:26.112
Did you take a bite
out of this donut?

17:26.180 --> 17:27.781
Yeah, it was from a
box on the counter.

17:27.848 --> 17:29.049
So what?
How long ago?

17:29.116 --> 17:30.183
I don't know. Five minutes?

17:30.251 --> 17:31.501
There's still time.

17:32.703 --> 17:35.572
(gagging)

17:35.640 --> 17:38.458
(coughing) God, Stewie, are you
out of your mind?

17:38.526 --> 17:40.594
Trust me, I'm only doing
what's best for you.

17:40.661 --> 17:43.213
Well, I do feel pretty
thin and wonderful.

17:43.281 --> 17:44.814
And I still got
to eat the donut.

17:44.882 --> 17:46.232
Why isn't everybody
doing this?

17:46.300 --> 17:47.951
(doorbell rings)
They are.

17:50.204 --> 17:51.955
I've got a package here
for Brian Griffin.

17:52.023 --> 17:53.039
Oh, that's me.

17:53.107 --> 17:54.541
Brian, no!

17:57.695 --> 17:59.446
Stewie, what the hell
is going on?

17:59.513 --> 18:01.181
I'm so sorry, Brian.

18:01.248 --> 18:03.099
Penelope told me
I had to kill you

18:03.184 --> 18:04.584
because you said
we should break up,

18:04.652 --> 18:06.252
but I couldn't bring myself
to do it.

18:06.320 --> 18:08.655
So then she said
she was gonna kill you and...

18:08.723 --> 18:11.157
This-this is not for you.

18:12.393 --> 18:13.460
That was weird.

18:13.527 --> 18:14.628
W-What was he doing?

18:14.695 --> 18:16.346
Anyway, Penelope's
trying to kill you!

18:16.414 --> 18:18.081
I told you she was bad news.

18:18.149 --> 18:19.749
Look, let's just get you
someplace safe.

18:21.152 --> 18:22.402
Dude, get out of here.

18:25.439 --> 18:28.041
Stewie, step aside.

18:28.109 --> 18:29.993
Penelope,
I can't let you do this.

18:30.061 --> 18:31.361
Stewie, she's
one year old.

18:31.445 --> 18:32.679
I think I can
handle this myself.

18:36.584 --> 18:38.585
All right, Stewie, tag in.

18:45.893 --> 18:50.030
Slo-o-w mo-o-o-tion
di-i-ving at yo-o-u!

19:08.182 --> 19:09.616
(yells)

19:09.683 --> 19:10.817
Anti-gravity gun!

19:10.868 --> 19:12.685
This is beyond my technology.

19:12.737 --> 19:14.621
Perhaps if I detonate
an electromagnetic pulse,

19:14.688 --> 19:15.688
it will disable it.

19:22.029 --> 19:24.297
(grunting, groaning)

19:41.148 --> 19:42.181
(yells)

19:56.196 --> 19:57.196
(yells)

20:09.408 --> 20:11.427
Stay away from my dog.

20:11.511 --> 20:13.545
Very well, Stewie. I shall.

20:13.596 --> 20:15.180
But just one thing.

20:15.248 --> 20:16.131
What?

20:25.225 --> 20:26.692
(gasps)

20:31.197 --> 20:33.031
(horn honks)

20:38.138 --> 20:39.571
That was...

20:39.639 --> 20:41.306
beautiful.

20:41.374 --> 20:43.575
I'm gonna tell my friends
I banged her.

20:49.299 --> 20:50.916
Hey, thanks for
saving my life.

20:50.984 --> 20:52.568
Well, it was the least
I could do.

20:52.635 --> 20:55.387
Obviously, it turns out
you were right about Penelope.

20:55.455 --> 20:56.588
You okay?

20:56.656 --> 20:57.856
I will be.

20:57.924 --> 20:59.191
I will be, babe.

20:59.259 --> 21:00.359
Oh, hey, Meg.

21:00.426 --> 21:01.510
What have you been up to?

21:01.511 --> 22:02.511
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru